ate","object_canonical":"2026-09-01t12:04:42.874z"},{"subject":"CVE-2026-56208","predicate":"description","object":"A heap buffer overflow vulnerability was found in libaom, the reference AV1 codec implementation. A flaw in the AV1 encoder's Look-Ahead Processing (LAP) mode causes the first-pass stats ring buffer wrap-around guard to be bypassed when g_lag_in_frames is set to 1 or higher. This results in a 232-byte out-of-bounds write on every encoded frame after the second, corrupting adjacent heap objects. An attacker who can influence encoder configuration in a transcoding service or WebRTC session could exploit this to cause a denial of service (process crash) or potentially achieve code execution.","source":"cve","object_type":"string","object_canonical":"a heap buffer overflow vulnerability was found in libaom, the reference av1 codec implementation. a flaw in the av1 encoder's look-ahead processing (lap) mode causes the first-pass stats ring buffer wrap-around guard to be bypassed when g_lag_in_frames is set to 1 or higher. this results in a 232-byte out-of-bounds write on every encoded frame after the second, corrupting adjacent heap objects. an attacker who can influence encoder configuration in a transcoding service or webrtc session could exploit this to cause a denial of service (process crash) or potentially achieve code execution."},{"subject":"CVE-2026-56208","predicate":"product","object":"Red Hat Enterprise Linux 10.0 Extended Update Support","source":"cve","object_type":"string","object_canonical":"red hat enterprise linux 10.0 extended update support"},{"subject":"CVE-2026-56208","predicate":"product","object":"Red Hat Enterprise Linux 7 Extended Lifecycle Support","source":"cve","object_type":"string","object_canonical":"red hat enterprise linux 7 extended lifecycle support"},{"subject":"CVE-2026-56208","predicate":"product","object":"Red Hat Enterprise Linux 8","source":"cve","object_type":"string","object_canonical":"red hat enterprise linux 8"